From a606921bd2af2d3717b89cbf507a0d2d857d12fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:38:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/29] external textures: give the corpus/sweep C++ driver
 noisemaker-render's capability

Task 1 of 3. filter/text and synth/media refused in every sweep case on the
C++ side ("input resource is not produced") because noisemaker-dsl-cpu-case
had no way to supply an externalTexture-declared effect's bound input --
noisemaker-render already gained --input/--texture (an earlier, unrelated
landing), but the corpus driver never did.

tools/benchmark/run_cpp_case.cpp: new --external-texture NAME=WxH:HEX flag
(repeatable), decoding hex bytes via Surface::from_rgba8 and populating
ExecutionInputs::external_textures -- the same executor field
noisemaker-render already uses, so this is wiring, not new engine capability.
Deliberately NOT a PNG-file flag like noisemaker-render's --texture: this
driver's inputs are always synthesized in-process by sweep.py/corpus_lane.py,
so inline hex avoids a needless PNG round trip through a scratch file per
case, and reuses the exact {name,width,height,rgba8} shape
run_cpu_case.mjs's record.externalTextures already decodes via
api.Surface.fromRgba8 -- one JSON field, one hex string, no second encoding
anywhere in the path.

tools/benchmark/corpus_lane.py: record_flags() now emits one
--external-texture flag per record.externalTextures entry. Since neither of
the two static executable-corpus.json records for filter/text/synth/media
carries that field, this is a no-op for tests/test_dsl_corpus_parity.py --
confirmed by rerunning it (still OK, same authorityRefused pair). It only
activates for tools/parity/sweep.py, which already builds
record["externalTextures"] for the JS lane; both lanes now render from the
exact same bytes.

Verification -- proof of the capability alone (before the divergence found
and fixed below): tools/parity/sweep.py --effects filter/text,synth/media
--variants 20 went from cpp_refused_only on every case to a real render on
both lanes.

Divergence found and fixed once both lanes could finally render synth/media
for real (never possible before this task, since the C++ side always
refused): 3 of 20 variants' float32 surface diverged from the authority by
exactly one half-float ULP (2^-12) at a couple of pixels, RGBA8 still
byte-exact. Root cause, traced to source: renderer.js's
createCanonicalBindings() spreads `...uniforms` (buildBindings()'s raw,
unrounded params[name]) for every ordinary effect-parameter uniform and only
explicitly Math.fround()'s a few reserved names (time/seed/deltaTime/aspect/
aspectRatio/renderScale) -- confirmed by grep, zero Math.fround calls
anywhere in mediaInput's emitted kernel body. `imageSize` (a vec2 DSL
parameter) is therefore carried by the authority as a full, un-rounded JS
double all the way into getImage()/rotate2D()'s arithmetic; the typed
emitter bound it as `glsl::Vec2` (float lanes), narrowing one step earlier
than the authority ever does. Exactly the same bug class this port already
has a precedent and mechanism for -- classicNoisedeck's palette uniforms
carried as `glsl::DVec3` instead of `glsl::Vec3` (see
_CLASSIC_NOISEDECK_DOUBLE_PALETTE_CARRIERS) -- generalized one vec width
down for one uniform on one program outside classicNoisedeck:

- include/noisemaker/glsl_types.hpp: `using DVec2 = Vec<2, double>;`
  (Vec<N,T> is already generic; DVec3/DVec4 existed, DVec2 didn't).
- include/noisemaker/glsl_runtime.hpp: DVec2 added to the UniformValue
  variant.
- src/graph/executor.cpp: vector_width/validate_uniform_abi_shape/
  materialize_plan_value all learn "glsl::DVec2" alongside the existing
  DVec3/DVec4 cases -- the same generic, ABI-driven uniform materialization
  path classicNoisedeck's carrier already flows through, no new special
  case needed there.
- tools/glslcpp/emit_typed_cpp.py: new, narrowly-scoped
  _DOUBLE_PRECISION_VEC2_UNIFORM_CARRIERS = {("synth/media:mediaInput",
  "imageSize")} plus _double_precision_vec2_uniform_type (mirrors
  _classic_noisedeck_double_uniform_type exactly). Getting the local alias
  (`vec2 size = imageSize;`, read in getImage/rotate2D) to actually carry
  double precision needed two more pieces neither exists for the
  classicNoisedeck carrier (which never mixes its double vectors with an
  ordinary float vector in one expression): the local declaration itself
  needs the same DVec2 override
  (_double_precision_vec2_alias_declaration), and every binary op or
  compound assignment that mixes a `size`-derived (or, transitively, `size`-
  arithmetic-derived) subtree against an ordinary Vec2 operand needs the
  ordinary operand promoted to `glsl::DVec2(...)` explicitly in the emitted
  text, since GLSL itself has no implicit vec-vec precision conversion and
  neither does this port's operator set
  (_references_double_precision_vec2_alias walks the subtree;
  double_precision_vec2_alias_symbol_ids records which locals got the
  override so a later expression node can recognize a reference to one).
- tools/dsl/generate_backend_compatibility.py: the identical, independently
  duplicated carrier list and cpp_type override, kept in sync with
  emit_typed_cpp.py by construction (matching how the classicNoisedeck list
  is already duplicated there for the same reason).
- Regenerated in dependency order (typed_slice -> backend_compatibility
  fixed point -> compat sha re-pinned into 4 consumers -> effect_catalog ->
  registry/test_effect_catalog re-pinned -> executable-corpus ->
  compiler-oracle stream -> export-kit compat list): every diff outside
  hash-cascade churn is confined to the one (program, uniform) pair, cross-
  checked by grep after each step. compat-effects.json stays at 167 (no
  admission changed). tests/test_typed_slice.cpp's own hand-written
  imageSize fixture updated from glsl::Vec2 to glsl::DVec2 to match (one
  line; the OTHER task11 fixture binding imageStill float32-scalar `1.0f`
  to imageSize to prove fail-closed-on-wrong-type is unaffected, since a
  scalar is still the wrong type against either vector width).

Verification:
- tools/parity/sweep.py --effects filter/text,synth/media --variants 20
  (--no-chains) and again --variants 60 (chains included): 40/40 then
  120/120 byte_exact, 0 divergent, both RGBA8 and float32.
- Regression: swept all 167 now-admitted effects (1002 cases, --seed
  20260916, --variants 6) and diffed case-by-case against this same lane's
  pre-existing 166-effect/996-case baseline (from the prior scatter-dispatch
  commit): 0 cases regressed (byte_exact -> anything worse). 37 cases
  improved -- 5 are filter/text now rendering instead of refusing (this
  task); the rest are pre-existing effects whose divergence had already
  been fixed by the lanes/integ4 merge's scalar-uniform narrowing fix,
  newly visible here because this is the first full regression sweep run
  since that merge. Two pre-existing, unrelated float32-only divergences
  remain (synth/gradient, synth/mandala) -- confirmed present in the
  original base-commit (9edf5fb) baseline too, same bug class (an ordinary
  vec2/vec3 uniform likely needing the same double-carrier treatment) but
  out of this task's scope.
- python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_dsl_corpus_parity: OK, unchanged
  (167 records, same authorityRefused pair -- the static corpus fixture
  carries no externalTextures for either effect, so this test's own
  behavior is untouched by this change, only the sweep's).
- noisemaker-cpu-tests: 586 pass / 1 pre-existing unrelated failure
  (typed_classic_noise_oracle_metadata_is_complete_and_load_bearing, noted
  in prior commits).

